# Build context exclusions for the service images (ARCHITECTURE.md section 8.2).
#
# Every service Dockerfile does `COPY . .` because the Maven reactor spans backend/ and needs the
# generated contract sources alongside it. Without this file that copy also drags in node_modules,
# every target/ directory and the whole of .git — hundreds of megabytes per image build, re-sent to
# the daemon for each of the thirteen services.
#
# NOTE: contracts/generated/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is git-ignored build output, but the
# in-image Maven build runs with -Dbuf.skip=true (buf is not in the maven base image), so the
# generated Java has to arrive through the build context. The Dockerfiles fail fast with a readable
# message if it is missing.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Node
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/.vite
frontend/coverage
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results

# Maven / Java build output
**/target
**/*.class

# Generated bindings for the other two languages; only Java is compiled into the images.
contracts/generated/python
contracts/generated/typescript

# Local tooling and editor state
.idea
.vscode
**/*.iml
.claude
.toolchain

# Docs and scripts are not needed to build a service jar.
docs
*.md
!backend/*/README.md

# Runtime data that must never be baked into an image.
evidence
**/*.log
.env
.env.*
